{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/494462-help-with-touchstones","id":494462,"title":"Help with Touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-04-28T00:26:20-07:00","id":494462,"title":"Help with Touchstones","content":"So I'm skimming through the section in 2nd edition to do with Touchstones and how there is one to link your character to the Physical world and one to the Spiritual world. I read it as if having your Physical Touchstone for example is something that would lock you into the Physical more if you could spend on your time on it, just as the Spiritual Touchstone tears at your character to bring you closer to the Shadow, is that right?<br /> The examples given in the corebook are fairly shady... The Abuser was one I didn't quite grok. I can see how a character would see them as addictive and someone they could never really walk away from, though I dunno, seems like going through the First Change would have a person like that get left behind?<br /> Then I saw the example of a Locus, for the Spiritual Touchstones. I liked the idea of that... My old/current character from 1e is a Bone Shadow that is a spiritual defender of the local locus, I felt upgrading him to 2e, the Locus would be a great Touchstone, however the example there seemed all the tempting in rewarding with Essence, growing a close bond and all... It was like a completely different type of conflict to the Physical Touchstone as mentioned above.<br /> <br /> I seem to be kinda not getting something, so I'd like to hear from some people more about how these are supposed to work and clearer examples really. I felt like good Physical Touchstones would be a Work Career or perhaps Friends Since School, then Spiritual Touchstones may include 'Marked Pack Territory' or something. I felt the Locus was a good one but rather I'd have it that it's out some place in the back of beyond and away from people or 'the city' or something.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm asking for more info on what would make good one and what the general formula for making a unique one up might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T10:21:50-07:00","id":494988,"title":"","content":"Your examples seem pretty good. All you basically need is a connection to someone or something that keeps you grounded to your human/spirit side, and gives the ST a dramatic hook.<br /> <br /> The relationship doesn't have to be positive. The Abuser keeps your character anchored in flesh because he's a constant reminder of the life she left behind. A piece of her human past that refuses to leave her alone. The Future Self torments your character, showing her a version of herself she may not like, but believes she is destined to become. It keeps her anchored in spirit because it shows her a &quot;perfected&quot; version of herself, freed from the constraints of flesh, and drives her towards that eventuality, even if she sees that version as far from perfect now.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the relationship can be positive, as long as it can still create drama - The Ex makes your character fell good, he gives her a reason to want to maintain a normal human life, keeping her anchored because she won't let go. But she also knows that she could hurt him, even kill him, if she goes into a rage at the wrong time - that's why she broke up with him in the first place. The buddy spirit is a real friend. It shows your character the good things in a spirit's life, and indulging in them makes her feel whole, keeps her anchored to that wild and fun side. But sometimes it asks her to do things she knows she shouldn't. The scary thing is, deep down, she knows she wants to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T12:43:14-07:00","id":495094,"title":"","content":"I see, so along with being something tangeable that can be effected and also shift the character's equilibrium if they drop things to follow through with them, they also need a dramatic hook so the ST can call them up better. I think linking them to Aspirations would make the most in my eyes, as they call to mind roughly what I want my character to do in the current session (or campaign for the long term one) but also things that could be leveraged with the character in social manipulation. My character wants to learn how to create a fetish, so a rites-master could show them and that causes leverage... Maybe the rites-master wants something in return.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the extra clarification when it comes to working up Touchstones. I really like the idea of them (along with Blood and Bone as replacing virtues and vices), I'm currently upgrading my 1e Itheaur Bone Shadow, so I'm finding alot of choices for his Spirit Touchstone, less so for his Flesh Touchstone, he's the type that's kinda survivalist, living alone in the pack territory and acting as a Shadow seer and warding off bad spirits for the pack.<br /> <br /> Still, this just makes me consider more what he was before the First Change and parts of his life held in the Flesh realm beyond his Pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}